  "notes": [
    "Partial by design. The full concordances run to 511, 484 and 170 sections; inventing the rest would produce a table that looks authoritative and is wrong in places nobody could predict. Only mappings held with high confidence are listed, and anything absent resolves to 'no mapping known' rather than to a guess.",
    "'ingredients_changed' marks a pair where the replacement is not a renumbering. Those are the dangerous ones: a user who assumes equivalence gets the elements of the offence wrong, which is worse than having no mapping at all.",
    "Every consumer must surface `review_status`. A section mapping presented as settled law, when it was authored by a model, is exactly the kind of confident error this system exists to avoid."
